  "harf": {
    "word": "عجل",
    "display": "عِجْل",
    "hint": "A golden idol fashioned by the Children of Israel during Moses' absence on the Mountain — its hollow body was said to 'moo' at its misguided worshippers",
    "verseRef": "7:148",
    "arabicVerse": "وَٱتَّخَذَ قَوْمُ مُوسَىٰ مِنۢ بَعْدِهِۦ مِنْ حُلِيِّهِمْ عِجْلًۭا جَسَدًۭا لَّهُۥ خُوَارٌ ۚ أَلَمْ يَرَوْا۟ أَنَّهُۥ لَا يُكَلِّمُهُمْ وَلَا يَهْدِيهِمْ سَبِيلًا ۘ ٱتَّخَذُوهُ وَكَانُوا۟ ظَـٰلِمِينَ",
    "verse": "7:148 - And the people of Moses made, after [his departure], from their ornaments a calf - an image having a lowing sound. Did they not see that it could neither speak to them nor guide them to a way? They took it [for worship], and they were wrongdoers."
  },
  "deduction": {
    "title": "The Stone-Carvers of the Ancient Valley",
    "intro": "Imagine a civilization that rose in the rocky valleys of Arabia, skilled in carving magnificent homes from the mountainsides. They flourished with strength and artistry, yet their story is marked by a chilling defiance of divine warning. As you delve into their tale, you will uncover a people whose arrogance led to their utter annihilation. Who were they?",
    "clues": [
      "We inherited a land of rocky plains and towering cliffs, where we built our dwellings with unmatched skill.",
      "We were known for carving secure homes into the mountains, feeling safe from any harm.",
      "A messenger came to us from among ourselves, reminding us of Allah's favors and warning us of punishment.",
      "We demanded a sign, and a miraculous she-camel emerged from the rock, a clear test from Allah.",
      "We defied the warning and hamstrung the she-camel, mocking the messenger and challenging the punishment.",
      "A single blast overtook us in our homes, and by morning we lay prostrate, as if we had never lived there."
    ],
    "categories": {
      "identity": {
        "label": "Who Am I?",
        "options": [
          "People of Thamud",
          "People of 'Ad",
          "People of Madyan",
          "People of Nuh",
          "People of Lut"
        ],
        "answer": "People of Thamud"
      },
      "trial": {
        "label": "Trial/Event",
        "options": [
          "Hamstrung the she-camel",
          "Broke the Sabbath",
          "Worshiped the golden calf",
          "Killed the prophet sent to them",
          "Built a tower to reach the sky"
        ],
        "answer": "Hamstrung the she-camel"
      },
      "location": {
        "label": "Key Element",
        "options": [
          "The she-camel",
          "The Ark",
          "The staff",
          "The white hand",
          "The manna and quails"
        ],
        "answer": "The she-camel"
      },
      "outcome": {
        "label": "Outcome",
        "options": [
          "Destroyed by a blast",
          "Saved from destruction",
          "Turned into apes",
          "Drowned in the sea",
          "Swallowed by the earth"
        ],
        "answer": "Destroyed by a blast"
      }
    },
    "verseRef": "69:5",
    "arabic": "فَأَمَّا ثَمُودُ فَأُهْلِكُوا۟ بِٱلطَّاغِيَةِ",
    "verse": "So as for Thamūd, they were destroyed by the overpowering [blast]. (69:5)"
